 "transcriber_notes": "SnowPilot chart (JPG export, 994x840 raster). Height axis in the middle, 6.12 px/cm; boundaries 61, 50, 45, 38, 27 (+-0.3 cm; bar edges and table lines agree). Hardness bars grow leftward on a non-uniform axis (ticks F 435, 4F 399, 1F 351, P 255, K 111, I 63 px, with third-class minor ticks at 439 (F-), 427/411, 387 px and so on), read against the ticks; the 97-61 cm bar slants from the F tick at the top to the F- tick at the bottom. Temperatures from the red dots on the top axis (-10 to 0 degC, ticks every degree, 43.3 px per degree, 0 at the height axis), read between neighbouring ticks; the 0 cm dot sits on the frame (+-0.1 degC). Densities printed at the top of each table row. No stability tests drawn. PF 90 copied as printed, although a boot could not pass the K crust at 38-27 cm, so it may be mistyped or a height. The Notes say the pit was dug in the flat meadow beside the study plot."
